The case split and the cube cover are complete, and no path in drive.py lets a leaf count as verified for a CNF other than base + its units, or without the exact cake_lpr line. All the defects below affect liveness or reporting, not soundness. Rung 36 is NOT closed yet: at 12:31 KST, 9 of 64 case-A leaves pass every check, 0 of the 32 B backup cubes have run, and the monolithic case-B run is still going (LRAT 1,607,487,488 bytes after 21 min).
(1) ALL:36 in addrows.py encodes 'at most 36 of the 56 occupancy variables are true' (sequential counter over all states, overflow clause at j = 36). 'At least 36' comes from owner.py family K with N = 36: at most 56 - 36 = 20 holes. Together: exactly 36 occupied. That is enough for M(5;7) <= 35 by heredity: every 36-subset of a valid set is valid, and v -> I(v) is injective, so the number of points equals the number of occupied states. S1 = {f1 <= 4} (35 states) and B2 = {f1 = 5} (21 states) partition the 56 states, so r + t = 36 gives r <= 13 or t <= 22; r >= 14 and t >= 23 would need 37 points. A valid 36-point set satisfies case A if r <= 13 and case B if t <= 22, because one-sided counters are satisfied by the prefix counts whenever count <= bound (checked by reading both counter codes).
(2) Checked independently (EXACT; scripts in <scratch>/agents/r36-audit/):
- both base CNFs match the recorded SHA-256 (aba65111..., 08b8ea9c...) and end with a newline;
- headers 457,857 / 5,569,648 and 457,842 / 5,569,618; nv = number of named variables;
- occ[s] = 32759 + s for all 56 states in both names.pkl;
- the row specs are exactly A {S1:25, S2:25, B1:16, B2:13, ALL:36} and B {S1:22, S2:25, B1:16, B2:16, ALL:36}, with families equal to my own re-derivation;
- ORDER A = all 21 B2 states; ORDER B = 20 of the 35 S1 states.
(3) drive.py:
- the top split runs m over range(1<<k), so it covers all 2^6 (A) and 2^5 (B) sign patterns of ORDER[:k];
- a timed-out cube becomes cube+x and cube-x on the next unused state; jobs are never deleted;
- state.json at 12:22 and 12:31: per case, leaves pairwise disjoint and sum 2^-|cube| = 1 (EXACT). Soundness of a cube split does not depend on what the split variables mean;
- write_cube keeps nv, raises the clause count by |units|, copies the body verbatim and appends '%d 0\n' per unit. All 12 cube CNFs on disk at 12:26 hash equal to base + units regenerated by my own code, and the recorded cnf_sha of all 9 verified leaves equals the regenerated hash;
- a verdict counts only on a stripped stdout line equal to 's VERIFIED UNSAT'; CaDiCaL rc 20 alone gives only 'unsat'. reverify.py uses the same test after re-hashing CNF and LRAT against the first-check row.

Nothing checks the monolithic case-B run. The bash -c wrapper only writes 'exit=$?' to run/c36_tle22.out, with no cake_lpr step, no time limit and no nice. A separate cake_lpr run is needed, with the heap sized to the proof:
- the LRAT is already 1.61 GB at 21 min;
- the 13 Nov 5.23 GB proof failed at 2,600 MB;
- the N = 37 proof of 5.26 GB passed at 4,200 MB;
- the SYNTHESIS spec is heap 4,300 then 4,600 MB and at least 6.2 GB resident;
- the CaDiCaL 3.0.1 proof may well be larger.
verify_cover.py expects the output at run/c36_tle22.cake; record the LRAT SHA-256 next to it. The 32 B backup cubes stay queued behind case A and will use CPU unless the owner holds them (NOSTART, LANES or a state edit) once the monolithic proof is checked.

novelty_md:
**Novelty.** For M(5;7) <= 35 (equivalently N(7;5,7) <= 35, or B6 <= 36 in Javůrek's notation), no matching prior result was found in the sources inspected.

Sources (as reported by NOVELTY20261113B sections 3, 6, 10 and C4, quoted in ETV7SAT section 9.1, and by ETV7SAT section 9; searches of 13 November 2026):
- Baek, arXiv:2206.04260;
- Baek-Balko, SoCG 2025;
- Schroeder v1 (19 Sep 2026);
- Javůrek, Figshare 34875984 (1 Nov 2026);
- Krapivin-Przybocki-Heule, arXiv:2607.02958;
- Balko-Valtr 2015/2017 and their data page;
- gotrevor/es7-ladder;
- GLitchfield experiment 0112;
- jcpaik/erdos-tuza-valtr.

What those sources say:
- No source has an upper bound on M(5;7) below 41.
- 41 itself is one substitution into Javůrek's Lemma 3 (16 + 25, must-cite), although the number is not printed. Refereed statements alone give 16 + 35 = 51; cup-cap gives 56; the lower bound is 26 (ETV construction, also found by PointSAT).
- Three public efforts leave 27 points open: gotrevor estimates >= 811 CPU h and did not run it; Javůrek ran a 28-point pilot with timeouts and one unchecked sub-case; GLitchfield writes "No upper bound is claimed".
- The project's own 40, 39, 37 and 36 were not found in the literature (bounded search, not a priority claim).
- Javůrek's Lemma 2 isolates the same quantity (B6 - 1 = M7(5,7)) and must be cited. Every component of the method has precedent: Chvátal-Komlós, Schroeder's Lemma 5.1 and Appendix B, and SAT on signotopes or triple orientations (Balko-Valtr, Scheucher, Heule-Scheucher, Krapivin-Przybocki-Heule).
- For the colouring form, NOVELTY says the comparison with Balko-Valtr's colouring model is still needed (ETV7SAT section 9.1).

Not covered:
- NOVELTY20261115 contains no statement on M(5;7) (grep).
- No literature search after 13 November 2026 is recorded, and this audit did no web search. The sources are 8 days old for this claim.
